TestGates: SDD

Purpose:
  Define test gate criteria. Every task MUST pass required test gates
  before advancing to DONE. Test gates are checkpoints, not separate
  stages — they are evaluated within the QA stage.

Owns: ./

Gates:

  BDD:
    must_pass:
      - all BDD scenarios pass
      - acceptance criteria met
      - no pending scenarios
    may_pass:
      - skipped scenarios with approved reason
    block:
      - failing BDD scenario for critical behavior
    owner: QA/Business

  Unit:
    must_pass:
      - all unit tests pass
      - coverage >= project threshold
      - no flaky tests
    may_pass:
      - known flaky tests with waiver
    block:
      - failing unit test for critical path
    owner: Implementer

  Integration:
    must_pass:
      - all integration tests pass
      - no broken contracts
      - database migrations work
    may_pass:
      - environment-specific failures with approved exception
    block:
      - failing integration test for critical path
    owner: Implementer/QA

  API:
    must_pass:
      - all API tests pass
      - contract tests pass
      - no breaking changes
    may_pass:
      - versioned breaking change with migration path
    block:
      - breaking change without versioning
      - failing API test for public endpoint
    owner: QA/BE

  Contract:
    must_pass:
      - all contract tests pass
      - consumer contracts verified
      - provider contracts verified
    may_pass:
      - pending consumer update with approved plan
    block:
      - broken contract without migration plan
    owner: QA/BE

  E2E:
    must_pass:
      - all E2E tests pass
      - critical user flows work
      - no regression in critical paths
    may_pass:
      - non-critical E2E failures with approved exception
    block:
      - failing E2E for critical user flow
    owner: QA

  UI:
    must_pass:
      - all UI tests pass
      - visual regression within threshold
      - accessibility checks pass
    may_pass:
      - minor visual differences with approved exception
    block:
      - broken UI for critical user flow
      - accessibility violation for critical path
    owner: FE/QA

  Mobile:
    must_pass:
      - all mobile tests pass
      - offline behavior works
      - push notifications work
    may_pass:
      - platform-specific issues with approved exception
    block:
      - broken mobile flow for critical feature
    owner: MD/QA

  Performance:
    must_pass:
      - response time within NFR
      - throughput meets target
      - resource usage within limits
    may_pass:
      - performance degradation with approved exception
    block:
      - response time > 2x NFR
      - throughput < 50% of target
    owner: QA/DO

  Load:
    must_pass:
      - system handles expected load
      - no resource exhaustion
      - graceful degradation
    may_pass:
      - load issues with approved scaling plan
    block:
      - system unavailable under expected load
      - resource exhaustion under normal load
    owner: QA/DO

  Security:
    must_pass:
      - all security tests pass
      - no critical/high vulnerabilities
      - security acceptance criteria met
    may_pass:
      - medium findings with accepted risk
    block:
      - critical/high vulnerability
      - security acceptance criteria not met
    owner: SC/QA

GateCalculation:
  Overall gate status:
    PASS: all required gates pass
    CONDITIONAL: some gates have accepted exceptions
    FAIL: any required gate fails

  A task MUST NOT advance to DONE while any required gate is FAIL.
  CONDITIONAL gates require explicit human approval.

Waiver:
  A test MAY be waived with:
    Waiver ID: WAIV-001
    Reason: <why waived>
    Owner: <who approved>
    ApprovedBy: human
    Expires: <date>
    Compensating control: <what replaces the test>

  Waived tests are tracked in @instances/vkard.az/testing/exceptions/.

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/testing.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestTypes: @types.sdd
  BDD: @bdd.sdd
  Unit: @unit.sdd
  Integration: @integration.sdd
  API: @api.sdd
  Contract: @contract.sdd
  E2E: @e2e.sdd
  UI: @ui.sdd
  Mobile: @mobile.sdd
  Performance: @performance.sdd
  Load: @load.sdd
  ProjectTesting: @instances/vkard.az/testing/INDEX.sdd
  ProjectFailures: @instances/vkard.az/testing/failures/
  ProjectExceptions: @instances/vkard.az/testing/exceptions/

State: +
  Note:
  Test gates are evaluated within the QA stage of the workflow.
  They are not separate stages themselves. A task advances from
  QA to SC only when all required test gates pass.
